# IMSI (MCC+MNC) -> APN. Consulted ONLY when a blank APN fails to attach.
#
# This table is an optimisation, not the primary path. A blank APN requests the
# subscription default, which 3GPP guarantees the HSS/UDM supplies (TS 27.007 10.1.1,
# TS 29.272), so it is self-correcting across every carrier, MVNO and travel eSIM. A
# *guessed* APN is not: it yields ESM cause #27 or silently attaches to the wrong PGW.
#
# Therefore: only rows verified High-confidence in docs/apn-reference.md appear here.
# Low-confidence travel-eSIM rows deliberately stay documentation. In particular there
# is NO generic "internet" fallback - it is a real APN on some networks and rejected on
# others, which would turn a working blank attach into a failure.
#
# Chinese IoT SIMs broadcast the same MCC-MNC as consumer SIMs, so this table cannot
# distinguish them and will confidently pick the wrong APN; blank-first is what saves us.
#
# Format: <mccmnc> <apn>

